{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`rebar bridge fsck` reports `store_integrity=13` on every canary run (stable across\n2026-08-10T21:16Z, 2026-08-10T22:13Z, 2026-08-11T22:16Z, and re-measured 2026-08-12).\nAll 13 findings are kind `reverse_missing_forward`: `.bridge_state/bindings.json` holds\n`reverse[<jira_key>] = <local_id>` for REB-410…REB-422 with no matching\n`bindings[<local_id>]`. Every referenced local ticket is `deleted` `ZZ-*TEST` fixture\nscaffolding created under a retired environment (`env_id ade0f2ef-…`, not this store's\n`01a1a015-…`). The drift keeps this bug ticket open and keeps the binding-drift canary\nalerting, masking any genuine future integrity fault behind a known-benign 13.\n\nThe operator has decided the remediation, verbatim: **\"delete.\"** — remove the orphaned\nreverse keys outright rather than tombstoning them into `bindings-retired.json`.\n\n## Approach\n\nDelete the 13 orphaned `reverse` entries through rebar's own library surface, then deliver\nthe change with the sanctioned tracker-commit door. No ad-hoc raw git in the tracker.\n\n1. Load the store via `BindingStore` (`rebar._engine.rebar_reconciler.binding_store`).\n2. Delete exactly the reverse keys whose forward entry is absent, asserting the computed\n   orphan set equals the expected 13 (REB-410…REB-422) before any mutation — so the repair\n   cannot act on a set that drifted since diagnosis.\n3. Persist with `BindingStore.save()` (tempfile + `os.replace`, atomic).\n4. Commit and push with `rebar._store.push.commit_and_push_tickets_branch(strict=True)` —\n   the helper `docs/concurrency.md` §\"Mutating the tracker\" names for committing pending\n   tracker content under the store write lock.\n\nWhy this door and not another: `tracker-maintenance --clean` repairs only stranded index\nentries and foreign top-level paths, and `rebar fsck --repair` only rebuilds ticket event\nsnapshots — neither can express a binding-store edit. `BindingStore.unbind()` cannot express\nit either: it pops `reverse` only when the forward entry still carries a `jira_key`\n(`binding_store.py:426-430`), and the missing forward entry is precisely the fault. That\nasymmetry is the mechanism that leaked these keys in the first place; it is recorded on this\nticket as a reusable finding but is a separate code change, out of scope for this data repair.\n\nSafety: a pre-repair backup of `bindings.json` is taken, and the tickets branch is verified\nclean with zero unpushed commits before the write, so the prior commit is itself a rollback\npoint.\n\n## Scope\n\nNo `src/` changes. This is a pure data repair of tracker state on the `tickets` branch:\n\n- `.tickets-tracker/.bridge_state/bindings.json` — delete 13 keys from the `reverse` map.\n\nNothing else is touched: `bindings` (forward) is unmodified, `bindings-retired.json` is\nunmodified (none of the 13 appear there), and no ticket events are written.\n\n## Testing\n\nDeterministic before/after verification against the live store; there is no new code to\nunit-test.\n\n- **Before:** `rebar bridge fsck --output json` → `store_integrity` = 13, all alerting\n  `binding_drift` cells 0. Direct store read → `bindings`=2111, `reverse`=2124, delta 13.\n- **Failure/edge path guarded:** the repair asserts the recomputed orphan set is exactly\n  {REB-410…REB-422} and aborts without writing if it differs, and asserts the store contains\n  no *other* reverse orphan (verified: total reverse orphans = 13, no more).\n- **After:** re-run `rebar bridge fsck --output json` → `store_integrity` = 0 and alerting\n  `binding_drift` cells still 0; direct read → `reverse` count drops by exactly 13 to 2111,\n  `bindings` unchanged at 2111, delta 0.\n- **No collateral:** confirm the forward map and `bindings-retired.json` are byte-identical\n  before and after.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The 13 orphaned `reverse` entries REB-410…REB-422 are deleted from\n      `.bridge_state/bindings.json`, and the forward `bindings` map and\n      `bindings-retired.json` are unchanged.\n- [ ] `rebar bridge fsck` reports `store_integrity` = 0 with all alerting `binding_drift`\n      cells empty.\n- [ ] The repair is performed through rebar's library + `commit_and_push_tickets_branch`,\n      with no ad-hoc raw git in the tracker, and the change is committed and pushed to\n      `origin/tickets`.\n- [ ] Before/after fsck evidence and the operator's delete decision are recorded as comments\n      on this ticket."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786532007720777001,"uuid":"b3b4ad97-a7ab-45cb-b155-670f54bd07d2"}